<div class="wp-block-uagb-container uagb-block-dc814105">
<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"animals","style":{"spacing":{"margin":{"top":"0","bottom":"0"}}}} -->
<h2 id="animals" class="wp-block-heading" style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0">Animals with lives of their own.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"spacing":{"margin":{"top":"0","bottom":"0"}}}} -->
<p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0">Deer, elk, foxes, rabbits, squirrels, bears, quail, owls, hawks and more. Each one gets hungry, tired, scared and curious, and does something about it: grazes, naps, wanders off, keeps clear of a lit campfire. The owls come out at night.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"spacing":{"margin":{"top":"0","bottom":"0"}}}} -->
<p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0">The server runs the animals, so everyone sees the same deer in the same place.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
</div>
<!-- /wp:uagb/container -->
